ARM 1  a ONE-output derivation, and the site computing the stride itself
       (this is the construction 48:331-336 needs, and 47_probes/p2b is not it:
        p2b projects a stride an impl wrote down, it does not recompute one)
       W13 Cold    site says  13
       W13 Warm    site says  16
       compiles gate-free. so under Reading B, stride is recoverable and the
       criterion demotes it. the collapse 48 reports is real.

ARM 2  what the recomputation actually is: the packing rule, at the site
       W13 Grid4   site says  13   truth  16   WRONG by 3
       W12 Grid4   site says  12   truth  12   agrees, which is how a sampled test
                                              reports green over a broken rule

ARM 3  the repair: put the grid on the strategy marker
       W13 Grid4   site says  16   truth  16   correct
       the fact did not disappear. it moved from the derivation's result onto the
       strategy, where it is still a fact the derivation supplies.

ARM 4  a sixth strategy whose packing is not a grid
       W13 Tagged  site says  13   truth  14   WRONG again
       so the repair in ARM 3 was a bet on the shape of the next strategy, not a
       removal of the fact. under an open strategy set (INTENTS I1) every such bet
       is a fact the derivation owes and the site is guessing at.
